# Kiln's engine signatures: 231 game functions Kiln finds by their bytes that emf_signatures.patterns (next to this
# file) does not have, one per line in EMF's pattern format (docs/modding/reference.md, v14 find_pattern;
# src/common/pattern_file.h). MIT licence (Kiln contributors): use them in any loader.
# Generated from Kiln's signature database (https://github.com/frostdev-ops/kiln, sigdb/symbols/, Kiln
# 0.2.0-dev.27, commit 14bcce2c5324): do not edit by hand; a fix belongs in Kiln's database.
# Check them against a game exe without starting the game:
#   emf_sigcheck --patterns kiln_signatures.patterns "<game>\enshrouded.exe"
# Each pattern must match exactly once in the exe's .text. `offset=N` alone: the function starts at match + N.
# `offset=N ; rel32`: the function is the target of the call or jump whose rel32 is at match + N.
# Names are Kiln's (`<service>/<Name>`), so a line can be looked up in Kiln's database; none equals a name in
# emf_signatures.patterns. The second comment line, where there is one, names the Kiln definition the pattern
# comes from when it is not the function's own first one, and Kiln's other names for the same function ("also").
# A pattern is Kiln's own, with its typed holes written as ??; nothing else was changed.
# What is here: every named address in Kiln's database that is a function's first byte, that EMF's file does not
# have (the same RVA on the same exe: 54 functions are in both and stay out), and that one pattern of Kiln's finds
# under the rule above on every exe below. Not here: 46 addresses inside functions (hook sites, return
# addresses), 6 data addresses, and 9 functions without one pattern for every exe (Kiln finds them inside
# another function, or with different bytes on the client and the server, or they are in the server's exe only).
# The comment above a line gives the function's RVA on each build it was checked on: the pattern matches once
# there and gives the address Kiln's own resolver gives ("s": the dedicated server's exe; "client only": Kiln
# has no such function for the server and the pattern does not match there). All patterns match once in the
# game client's exe of both builds.
# Checked builds (the game's "Build version", the exe's sha256); the older builds that emf_signatures.patterns
# lists were not checked:
#   1285601  ce6fdba63e27744943b695921383a29133285d359e07671f6ca33a47e2147618
#   1285601s c5c9fe50c6398d2adedd98923c2d04bf9d9b4af64c1447ac167cdf8f874ff84f
#   1287369  5d9ef2f140b8ed49e30dbee655841b89d08baec20f799a1817e171a18a850c77
#   1287369s f0d824be7fcd48ebfe2458ff5c28da26060c2074e3ec1fcac587e5a1d508aeb2

# IsLocalPlayer: 1285601=0x3bb660 1287369=0x3bb740 (the server's exe: not in Kiln's database)
IsLocalPlayer = CC 39 4A ?? 0F 94 C0 C3 CC ; offset=1

